        "section": [
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">COPD exacerbation, treated with bronchodilators and steroids</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you regarding your patient, an 86-year-old male admitted on 27/09/2002 with an acute exacerbation of his known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, he presented with increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced exercise tolerance. Clinical examination revealed bilateral expiratory wheeze. Chest X-ray confirmed hyperinflation without evidence of pneumonia or pneumothorax. Arterial blood gas analysis demonstrated mild hypoxaemia. Spirometry confirmed severe airflow obstruction consistent with his known COPD. He was treated with nebulised bronchodilators (salbutamol and ipratropium), a short course of systemic corticosteroids, and supplemental oxygen therapy. His condition improved satisfactorily and he was discharged on 28/09/2002 in a stable condition. Please continue inhaled maintenance bronchodilator therapy and ensure timely pulmonary rehabilitation review. Kind regards, Dr. [Hospital Physician]</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
